XSD Overview
XSD

!!!Introduction

XSD is a group of four parts under <[XSD/]> in the namespace <[Poco::XSD]>: an object model of
XML Schema documents, a parser for XML Schema and WSDL documents, the <*XSDGen*> code generator
and a validator that checks XML documents against an XML Schema at run time. <*XSDGen*>
generates C++ classes from XML Schema and WSDL documents; it is the inverse of the XML Schema
generator in <*RemoteGenNG*>, which generates XML Schema and WSDL documents from C++ classes.


!!!Components

!!Types

The <*Types*> library (<*PocoXSDTypes*>, namespace <[Poco::XSD::Types]>) holds the object model
of XML Schema documents: schemas, elements, types, attributes and groups. The class
<[TypesManager]> keeps all loaded schemas. It is process-wide and not synchronised as a whole:
load schemas, fix them up and generate code from one thread at a time.

Dependencies: Foundation, XML.

!!Parser

The <*Parser*> library (<*PocoXSDParser*>, namespace <[Poco::XSD::Parser]>) parses XML Schema
and WSDL documents into the object model of the <*Types*> library.
Referenced schemas (<[schemaLocation]>) are opened through <[Poco::URIStreamOpener]>, so an
application that loads schemas over HTTP or HTTPS registers
<[Poco::Net::HTTPStreamFactory]> or <[Poco::Net::HTTPSStreamFactory]> itself.
Locations named in <[schemaLocation]> and WSDL import attributes are opened with the
privileges of the process through every registered URI scheme, so schemas and WSDL documents
must come from a trusted source.

Dependencies: Types, XML, Foundation.

!!XSDGen

<*XSDGen*> (built from <[XSD/CodeGen]>) generates C++ classes with Remoting attributes from
XML Schema and WSDL documents. The generated classes are passed to <*RemoteGenNG*>, which
generates the code for SOAP clients and servers. When built with NetSSL (compile definition
<[POCO_XSD_ENABLE_HTTPS]>, set by CMake when a NetSSL library is part of the build),
<*XSDGen*> also retrieves schemas over HTTPS.
The [[00205-XSDGenUserGuide.html XSDGen User Guide]] describes its configuration and use.

Dependencies: Types, Parser, XML, Util, Net, Foundation; NetSSL for HTTPS.

!!Validator

The <*Validator*> library (<*PocoXSDValidator*>, namespace <[Poco::XSD::Validator]>) validates
an XML document against an XML Schema at run time. It is based on libxml2 and does not depend
on the other three parts. <[Validator::validate(xml, xsd)]> throws
<[Poco::DataFormatException]> when the schema does not parse, the document is not
well-formed, or the document violates the schema.
The document may come from an untrusted source; documents with a document type declaration
are rejected. The schema must not: its entities are expanded (with libxml2 before 2.13 also
external entities, which can read local files), and schemas that import or include other
schemas by location are resolved through libxml2's default resource loader, which can read
local files; with libxml2 before 2.13, diagnostics about such schemas may be written to
standard error. <[Validator::validate()]> keeps no shared state and may be called
concurrently.

Dependencies: Foundation, libxml2.


!!!Building XSD

!!CMake

The CMake options <*ENABLE_XSD_TYPES*>, <*ENABLE_XSD_PARSER*> and <*ENABLE_XSD_CODEGEN*> are
on by default and off with <*POCO_MINIMAL_BUILD*>. <*ENABLE_XSD_VALIDATOR*> is off by default
and is turned off automatically when libxml2 is not found.

    cmake -B build -DENABLE_XSD_VALIDATOR=ON
    cmake --build build

libxml2 comes from the system: the package <[libxml2-dev]> on Debian and Ubuntu, the SDK on
macOS, and the vcpkg port <[libxml2]> on Windows.

!!GNU Make

The components <[XSD/Types]>, <[XSD/Parser]> and <[XSD/CodeGen]> are part of the default
build. The Validator and its test suite are built separately; <[make install]> does not copy
the Validator headers.

    make -C XSD/Validator
    make -C XSD/Validator/testsuite

With <[POCO_XSD_ENABLE_HTTPS=1]> in the environment, <*XSDGen*> is built with HTTPS support
against NetSSL_OpenSSL.


!!!Parsing a Schema

The following program loads the schema at the URI given on the command line (for example
<[file:///home/user/schema.xsd]> or an <[http]> URI), resolves its references and prints
the names of its top-level elements. <[Schema::types()]> returns the named types in the same way.

    #include "Poco/XSD/Parser/XSDContentHandler.h"
    #include "Poco/XSD/Types/TypesManager.h"
    #include "Poco/Net/HTTPStreamFactory.h"
    #include "Poco/URI.h"
    #include "Poco/Exception.h"
    #include <iostream>

    using Poco::XSD::Parser::XSDContentHandler;
    using Poco::XSD::Types::TypesManager;

    int main(int argc, char** argv)
    {
        if (argc != 2) return 1;
        Poco::Net::HTTPStreamFactory::registerFactory();
        try
        {
            XSDContentHandler::SchemaNSToLocationMap schemaMap;
            auto pSchema = XSDContentHandler::loadXSD(Poco::URI(argv[1]), schemaMap);
            TypesManager::instance().fixupSchemas();
            for (const auto& [name, pElement]: pSchema->elements())
                std::cout << name << std::endl;
        }
        catch (const Poco::Exception& exc)
        {
            std::cerr << exc.displayText() << std::endl;
            return 1;
        }
        return 0;
    }

The program links with PocoXSDParser, PocoXSDTypes, PocoXML, PocoNet and PocoFoundation.


!!!Validating a Document

<[Validator::validate()]> takes the XML document and the XML Schema as strings. It returns
when the document conforms to the schema and throws <[Poco::DataFormatException]> otherwise.

    #include "Poco/XSD/Validator/Validator.h"
    #include "Poco/Exception.h"
    #include <iostream>
    #include <string>

    bool isValid(const std::string& xml, const std::string& xsd)
    {
        try
        {
            Poco::XSD::Validator::Validator::validate(xml, xsd);
            return true;
        }
        catch (const Poco::DataFormatException& exc)
        {
            std::cerr << exc.displayText() << std::endl;
            return false;
        }
    }
